  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 81b9501dec89da64eb81f4c230bdd187, type: 3}
  m_Name: Night Vision
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HoneyAndHemlock.Customers.CustomerSO
  _requestedPotion: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7669af67348246f449881bbe75ccef0a, type: 2}
  _request:
  - I patrol the eastern wall every night and the lanterns have been guttering out
    all week. Something's wrong with the wax or something. Last night, I couldn't
    see my own hand in front of my face.
  - My eldest son went missing in the Darkwood three nights ago. Search parties can't
    go in after sundown. The trees swallow all the light. I need to find him myself,
    and I need to see when no one else can.
  _playerResponse:
  - Can't work in darkness
  - Let's fix those eyes
  _successfulResponse:
  - I can see everything. The cracks in the wall, a rabbit in the field, the tree
    line a hundred yards out. It's like someone lit the whole world on fire. I won't
    be falling off the wall tonight.
  - I can see the footprints. Even in the dark, the trail is as clear as midday!
    I'm going to find my boy. Thank you. Thank you for giving me a chance.
  _failedResponse:
  - Everything's blurry and there's a strange shimmer at the edges. And are those...
    are those colors I've never seen before? My eyes are doing something very odd.
  - It's worse. Now I see things in the dark that aren't there. Shapes. Moving shapes.
    I don't think this is helping me find my boy any faster.
  _cosmicResponse:
  - "I saw something in the dark that I wish I hadn\u2019t. Something enormous. I
    wish I could see that clearly in the dark when patrolling."
  - Oh the horror, the cosmic horror!! Oh, sorry. Right, my boy is still out there.
    I still need to see in the dark.
